---
import SocialLinks from '../components/SocialLinks.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Listed newest first.
const timeline = [
	{
		org: 'GIC',
		period: 'Jan 2024 – May 2026',
		role: 'Software Engineer',
		note: 'Funding & liquidity management for treasury',
	},
	{
		org: 'WSO2',
		period: 'Jun 2021 – Jul 2023',
		role: 'Software Engineer → Senior Software Engineer',
		note: 'Internal platforms, microservices and auth',
	},
	{
		org: 'DirectFN',
		period: 'Feb 2019 – Jun 2021',
		role: 'Software Engineer',
		note: 'Real-time trading and market data terminals',
	},
];
---

<Layout title="About" description={`${SITE.yearsInIndustry} years building business-critical software across trading, internal platforms and treasury.`}>
	<div class="container-page pt-14">
		<p class="label">/about</p>
		<h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">About</h1>

		<div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_18rem]">
			<!-- TODO: rewrite in your own voice. Keep it a story, not a CV. -->
			<div class="prose">
				<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed">
					I've spent the last {SITE.yearsInIndustry} years building business-critical software, mostly in finance,
					where the data has to be right and the people using it need it now.
				</p>

				<h2>DirectFN: real-time from day one</h2>
				<p>
					I started out building trading and market data applications for brokerages and capital markets firms.
					It was my introduction to real-time systems and to a domain where what's on the screen directly drives
					decisions about money.
				</p>

				<h2>WSO2: owning things end to end</h2>
				<p>
					At WSO2 I worked on the internal platforms the company runs on, across HR, finance and people
					operations. I took products from database to UI, broke large backends into smaller services, and worked
					on shared building blocks like authentication that other teams relied on. A lot of my
					<a href="/blog">blog posts</a> come from this period.
				</p>

				<h2>GIC: correctness in treasury systems</h2>
				<p>
					At GIC I worked on treasury systems that help portfolio managers handle funding and liquidity. The work
					was integration-heavy: moving orders between internal and external systems, keeping data consistent
					across many sources, and giving the business a live, trustworthy view of where things stand.
				</p>

				<h2>What I care about</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Simple, explicit designs</strong> that are easy to extend without breaking what's already there.</li>
					<li><strong>Treating failure as normal.</strong> Delays, retries and mismatches will happen, so the system should expect them.</li>
					<li><strong>Tests that catch real bugs</strong>, not just ones that make the coverage number go up.</li>
					<li><strong>Working closely with the business</strong>, from the first conversation about a feature to running it in production.</li>
				</ul>

				{/*
				<p>
					Outside work: TODO, a line or two about you as a person (it's what people remember from an about
					page).
				</p>
				*/}
			</div>

			<aside class="space-y-6">
				<div class="panel">
					<div class="panel-head">experience</div>
					<ol class="relative p-4">
						{
							timeline.map((t, i) => (
								<li class="relative border-l border-line pb-6 pl-5 last:pb-0">
									<span
										class:list={[
											'absolute top-1.5 -left-[4.5px] h-2 w-2 rounded-full',
											i === 0 ? 'bg-accent' : 'bg-line',
										]}
										aria-hidden="true"
									/>
									<p class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-fg">{t.org}</p>
									<p class="font-mono text-xs text-faint tabular">{t.period}</p>
									<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg">{t.role}</p>
									<p class="text-sm text-muted">{t.note}</p>
								</li>
							))
						}
					</ol>
				</div>
				<div class="panel p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-muted">Want to get in touch?</p>
					<SocialLinks class="mt-3" />
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
